WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.975 --> 00:00:05.030
(shimmering orchestral music)

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:07.170
- [Narrator] Ladakh, India
is home to one of the

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:09.793
highest optical telescopes in the world.

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:15.059
Its environment makes
it ideal for stargazing.

00:00:15.059 --> 00:00:17.830
(shimmering orchestral music)

00:00:37.611 --> 00:00:41.020
(light piano music)

00:00:49.521 --> 00:00:50.800
(light piano music)

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:52.940
- [Narrator] The Indian
Astronomical Observatory

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:55.730
is spread across 120 acres of land,

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:58.468
and located at the northern tip of India.

00:00:58.468 --> 00:01:00.220
(light piano music)

00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:11.460
- [Narrator] The
remoteness of its location

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:14.094
makes it ideal for astronomical study.

00:01:14.094 --> 00:01:17.511
(light orchestral music)  

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:48.470
(quiet rustling)

00:01:51.755 --> 00:01:53.320
(light piano music)

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:09.540
- [Narrator] The observatory's
altitude of approximately

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:11.580
two and a half miles above sea level

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:14.330
allows the scientists to
collect a wider range data

00:02:14.330 --> 00:02:16.930
than they would at lower levels.

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:19.620
But the isolated location
means that often,

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:21.380
the only other people the scientists and

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:24.363
engineers see are the occasional tourists.

00:02:30.981 --> 00:02:34.840
(slow, dramatic music)

00:02:44.715 --> 00:02:47.130
(light orchestral music)

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:49.660
- [Narrator] Whether you're
looking up as an astronomer,

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:54.053
or just a traveler, there's
no night sky quite like this.

00:03:01.976 --> 00:03:04.309
(soft beep)

